diff --git a/RIGGING.md b/RIGGING.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..465ee5d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/RIGGING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Rigging
+
+## Stack
+- language: JavaScript
+- runtime: browser
+- packageManager: npm
+
+## Directories
+- implementation: src
+- specs: features
+- verification: features/support
+- assets: assets
+- scantlings: none
+
+## Commands
+- discover: `npx cucumber-js --dry-run --tags "not @captain and not @shipwright"`
+- focused: `ref="{scenario}"; npx cucumber-js "${ref%%:*}" --name "^${ref#*:}$" --tags "not @captain and not @shipwright"`
+- broad: `npx cucumber-js --tags "not @captain and not @shipwright"`
+- coverage: none
+- step-usage: none
+- plank-inventory: none
+- typecheck: none
+- lint: none
+- conformance: none
+
+## Perturbation
+- message: `PERTURBATION: consider current durable context; remove when fixed`
+- perturb: `throw new Error("PERTURBATION: consider current durable context; remove when fixed");`
+
+## Tiers
+- default: @logic
+- sandbox: @sandbox
+- policy: happy-dom first; real-browser tier only when a specified behaviour cannot be observed under happy-dom
+- weather: none
+- runrecord: none
+
+## Dependencies
+- policy: locked
+- dependency: @cucumber/cucumber
+- dependency: happy-dom
+
+## Outbound
+- outbound: none
diff --git a/features/todo-app.feature b/features/todo-app.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ce58830
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-app.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,198 @@
+Feature: TodoMVC Application
+  As a user
+  I want a persistent todo list with filtering
+  So that I can track and manage tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the page is open
+
+  Rule: No todos
+
+  Scenario: Main section and footer hidden when no todos
+    When the page loads
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Rule: New todo
+
+  Scenario: Create a new todo
+    When I type "Buy groceries" in the new todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then "Buy groceries" is added to the todo list
+    And the new todo input is cleared
+    And the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is trimmed and empty input is rejected
+    When I type "   " in the new todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then no todo is added to the list
+    And the main section is hidden
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all marks all todos as complete
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title         | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | false     |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+    When I check the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos are marked as complete
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all unchecks all todos when all are complete
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title         | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | true      |
+      | Walk the dog  | true      |
+    When I check the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos are marked as active
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle all reflects individual todo state
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title         | completed |
+      | Buy groceries | false     |
+      | Walk the dog  | false     |
+    When I complete the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+    When I complete the todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Rule: Item
+
+  Scenario: Toggle a single todo complete
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then "Buy groceries" has the class "completed"
+    And the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Toggle a completed todo back to active
+    Given the completed todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When I click the toggle checkbox for "Buy groceries"
+    Then "Buy groceries" does not have the class "completed"
+    And the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Remove button visible on hover
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When I hover over the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then the destroy button for "Buy groceries" is visible
+
+  Scenario: Destroy a todo
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When I click the destroy button for "Buy groceries"
+    Then "Buy groceries" is removed from the todo list
+
+  Rule: Editing
+
+  Scenario: Activate editing mode
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy groceries"
+    Then "Buy groceries" enters editing mode
+    And the edit input is focused with value "Buy groceries"
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on Enter
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When I clear the edit input and type "Buy organic groceries"
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo title is updated to "Buy organic groceries"
+    And "Buy groceries" exits editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Save edit on blur
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When I clear the edit input and type "Buy organic groceries"
+    And I blur the edit input
+    Then the todo title is updated to "Buy organic groceries"
+    And "Buy groceries" exits editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Discard edit on Escape
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When I clear the edit input and type "Something else"
+    And I press Escape
+    Then the todo title remains "Buy groceries"
+    And "Buy groceries" exits editing mode
+
+  Scenario: Destroy todo on empty edit
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" is in editing mode
+    When I clear the edit input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then "Buy groceries" is removed from the todo list
+
+  Rule: Counter
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows pluralized active count
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Task one     | false     |
+      | Task two     | false     |
+      | Task three   | true      |
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+    When I complete the todo "Task one"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes finished todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task active | false     |
+      | Task done   | true      |
+    When I click the clear completed button
+    Then "Task done" is removed from the todo list
+    And "Task active" remains in the todo list
+    And the clear completed button is hidden
+
+  Rule: Persistence
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist to localStorage
+    Given the todo "Buy groceries" exists
+    When I complete the todo "Buy groceries"
+    Then localStorage key "todos-vanilla-js" contains a todo with title "Buy groceries" and completed true
+
+  Scenario: Todos load from localStorage on page reload
+    Given the page has stored two todos in localStorage
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then both stored todos are displayed in the todo list
+
+  Rule: Routing
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title      | completed |
+      | Active one | false     |
+      | Done one   | true      |
+    When I navigate to "#/"
+    Then all todos are visible
+    And the "All" filter link has the class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title      | completed |
+      | Active one | false     |
+      | Done one   | true      |
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then only "Active one" is visible
+    And the "Active" filter link has the class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title      | completed |
+      | Active one | false     |
+      | Done one   | true      |
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then only "Done one" is visible
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Todo hidden by filter disappears on state change
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title      | completed |
+      | Active one | false     |
+      | Done one   | true      |
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    And I complete the todo "Active one"
+    Then "Active one" is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
+    Given I navigate to "#/active"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the class "selected"
+    And only active todos are visible
